    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A federation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#guatemala">Guatemala</a>, El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#salvador">Salvador</a>, Honduras, Nicaragua and Costa Rica that broke away from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mexico">Mexico</a> in 1823.</li><li>Liberal reforms under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#francisco-morazan">Francisco Morazán</a> angered the Church and rural communities, while the federal government lacked money and an army.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rafael-carrera">Rafael Carrera</a>’s revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#guatemala">Guatemala</a> and the secession of the states destroyed the union by 1841, though the dream of unity lived on.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Central American federation abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#slavery">slavery</a> in 1824, more than forty years before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#united-states">United States</a> did so.</p></aside>
    </section>

